Depth-First Search (DFS)

Definition:
DFS explores as deep as possible along one path before backtracking.

Data Structure Used: Stack (LIFO) or Recursion

DFS Algorithm
Start from the source node.
Mark it as visited.
Visit one unvisited neighbor.
Continue until no unvisited neighbor exists.
Backtrack.
Repeat until all vertices are visited.



